# Repo-root ShellCheck config (honored only when shellcheck runs FROM the repo
# root, supported since ShellCheck v0.7 — CI and the README commands both do).
#
# SC2012: "Use find instead of ls" — info-level false positive for the simple
# existence check `ls <globs> | head -1 | grep -q .` in
# plugins/kit/.../detect-mode.sh. `find` is overkill there, and editing that kit
# script would trip version-sync's diff-aware bump guard for a cosmetic lint.
#
# Tradeoff (accepted): this is a repo-WIDE disable, so it silences SC2012
# everywhere, not just the one offending line. A scoped `# shellcheck
# disable=SC2012` directive inside detect-mode.sh would be narrower, but that
# edit lives under plugins/** and would demand a version bump for pure lint
# churn. The blast radius is acceptable: no other tracked script uses `ls` in a
# way SC2012 would (correctly) flag, so nothing real is being hidden.
disable=SC2012
